  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Clinique Vétérinaire du Careï, at 28 Val du Careï in Menton, was co-founded in 1994 by Drs Sandrine Franzolini and Werner Glavinaz, both graduates of the Alfort national veterinary school. Dr Fabrice Loumeau is part of the team. It is one team with the Carnoles clinic in Roquebrune-Cap-Martin (167 avenue Pasteur, 04 92 10 32 11), which shares the same website: "two sites, one team", according to the site's home page.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>According to the official website of the Careï and Carnoles clinics, the Careï clinic receives patients Monday to Friday from 8am to 12pm then from 2:30pm to 7pm, and on Saturday from 8:30am to 2pm (Carnoles: Saturday from 8:30am to 12pm). Phone: 04 92 10 03 00.</p>
      <p>The website presents a team of vets and specialised assistants, and details the services. The ultrasound machine lets the vets examine the abdomen, pelvis, neck and cardiovascular system, and monitor a pregnancy. The clinic has a surgical unit; for complex cases it refers to a specialist. For dentistry, an ultrasonic scaler and a polisher remove tartar; the site points out that 85% of dogs over two years old are affected by oral disease. Blood tests are done on site, with results in fifteen to twenty minutes, and the shop area (food for dogs, cats and small pets, parasite treatments, wormers, dental hygiene, shampoos, supplements) is on free access during opening hours.</p>
      <p>According to the Mappy directory, the clientele includes dogs, cats and small pets, and the clinic has reserved parking; neither point appears on the official website.</p>
      <p>Emergencies: the website's hours grid says "Nights, Sundays and public holidays: emergencies", and specifies that outside opening hours you are put through to "our emergency service" by calling 04 92 10 03 00 (Careï) or 04 92 10 32 11 (Carnoles); the website does not say who provides this service or until what time it answers.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: in Menton, at the far end of the department, it's best to have a reliable vet address in mind before heading off into the hinterland with your dog.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Menton town centre and its seafront are just a few minutes from the clinic.</p>
